---
description: VibeRaven launch check for AI-built apps on Vercel + Supabase (advice, not a gate)
alwaysApply: true
---

For an AI-built app on Vercel and Supabase, suggest `npx -y viberaven@1.6.3 check` before it launches or is handed off, after a Supabase migration or policy change, or when the user reports a production error about RLS, env vars, the database connection, the service role key or a Stripe webhook.

This is advice, not a gate: the user decides when to ship. It is a repository check, not a live database test.

Read `.viberaven/agent-tasklist.md` first, then `.viberaven/gate-result.json` and `.viberaven/mission-map.md`.
Fix one gap, then re-run `npx -y viberaven@1.6.3 check` once per batch. For a CI verdict: `npx -y viberaven@1.6.3 --strict`.

A clear `gate.status` covers the repo checks only; it is not a security audit.

Before editing these files, read `.viberaven/agent-context.md` and `.viberaven/mission-map.md`.

Full rules: `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` (installed by `npx -y viberaven@1.6.3 init --agents all`).